            <ArticleTitle>[The role of sexual trauma as a cause of orofacial symptoms. Case report].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>37-40</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Authors describe a 58-sitting psychotherapy of a 46-year-old female patient with psychogenic atypical facial pain. Sexual trauma in the childhood was found as a cause of the psychogenic pain symptoms, leading to series of unnecessary extraction of teeth in this case. Psychotherapeutic treatment led to the recovery of the somatic symptoms, and a moderate improvement of the behaviour related to men of this patient.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
